examination.exam_results:
PET scan after initial treatment showed complete metabolic response of vaginal carcinoma. MRI showed a 17 × 8.6 × 7.5 cm moderately defined heterogeneous region in the right vastus intermedius muscle and a 6.7 × 4.4 × 4.3 cm soft tissue mass in the vastus medialis muscle not involving femur but abutting neurovascular bundle, suggestive of sarcoma. Ultrasound-guided biopsy showed FNCLLCC grade 3 pleomorphic sarcoma with rhabdomyoblastic differentiation characterised by polygonal cells with voluminous eosinophilic cytoplasm and variable staining with SMA, desmin and MyoD1. FISH did not show MDM2 amplification, excluding dedifferentiated liposarcoma. Staging PET scan showed no nodal or distant metastases. Surgical specimen measured 130 × 100 × 80 mm, well demarcated intramuscular tumour adherent to femur with heterogeneous cut surface including solid fleshy tumour, haemorrhage, cystic degeneration and necrosis. Microscopy showed highly pleomorphic cells with solid and fascicular architecture, necrosis, brisk mitotic activity including atypical mitotic figures (up to 21 mitoses per 10 high power fields), rhabdomyoblastic differentiation with spindled and rounded rhabdomyoblasts with abundant voluminous eosinophilic cytoplasm, extensive reactivity for SMA and desmin. Tumour invaded femur cortical bone and marrow focally. Perineural invasion identified. Surgical margins were clear.'
